<item>
<title>[DEV-15671] Transcriptions: Ability to opt out at the call level</title>
<link>https://lspapp.atlassian.net/browse/DEV-15671</link>
<project id="10000" key="DEV">Development</project>
<description><h2><a name="Requirements%3A"></a>Requirements:</h2> <ol> <li>In the caller: add <b>ability to opt out</b> from AI transcriptions for specific call, <b><em>prior to the call</em></b></li> </ol> <ul> <li>Add an Icon next to Mute <ins><em>for Requestor Only</em></ins><br/> <span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/48571" alt="image-20241010-232434.png" width="22.953964194373402%" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></li> </ul> <p><a href="https://fontawesome.com/icons/square-quote?f=classic&amp;s=regular" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://fontawesome.com/icons/square-quote?f=classic&amp;s=regular</a> </p> <ul> <li>Icon should be available if: <ul> <li>1) User is a member of AI Policy, AND</li> <li>2) Service type selected is added to the policy, AND</li> <li>3) AI-supported language and communication type is selected.</li> </ul> </li> <li>Tooltip on enabled state: "Turn off transcription for the next call."</li> <li>Clicking this icon changes it to crossed. Transcriptions are now disabled <ul> <li>Tooltip on disabled state: "Turn on transcription for the next call."</li> </ul> </li> <li>Enabled by default if matching criteria (policy etc..)</li> <li>Selection is reset after each call and goes back to enabled</li> </ul> <ol> <li><b>During the call</b> <em>(Updated by Tanya</em> <b><em>after</em></b> <em>refinement to simplify the scope)</em><b>:</b></li> </ol> <ul> <li>If the user has not opted out of Transcription (based on step 1 above) Transcription icon in the caller starts pulsing once transcription has started <ul> <li>Tooltip on transcribed state: "Call is being transcribed"</li> <li>Visible for all participants on the call</li> </ul> </li> <li>Icon is clickable only for the meeting host (for on demand calls - this means only for requestor)</li> <li>Clicking on the icon as a requestor opens up a drop-down with text "AI Transcriptions and Summary have been enabled in this call." and a button "Stop Transcriptions" <ul> <li>When clicking "Stop Transcriptions" - show a confirmation dialog: "You will not be able to resume transcriptions once they are turned off. Are you sure you would like to proceed?" Buttons: "Cancel" / "Stop".</li> <li>After transcriptions are stopped, transcription icon is no longer available in the caller during the duration of this call.</li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p><b>Notes from Refinement:</b></p> <ul> <li>UI changes and some server-side work to send API call to AI Core</li> <li>could be few seconds delay between clicking 'stop' or 'start' and that action taking place (due to call/response to AI Core) <ul> <li>do we need to make user wait? show some confirmation that the action is done?</li> </ul> </li> <li>explore if there is a way to mute this AI participant through Twilio</li> <li>interpreter will not see icon in their caller</li> <li>do we get single summary with all parts in a stop/start scenario? or store as separate transcriptions? (<a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Ad005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" class="user-hover" rel="557058:d005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" data-account-id="557058:d005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" accountid="557058:d005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" rel="noreferrer">Tetiana Tymonina</a> ) <ul> <li><em><span class="error">&#91;Tanya&#93;</span></em>: N/A. Decided not to support pause/resume functionality.</li> </ul> </li> <li>do we need to show interpreter the icon for transcription/summary taking place? this should be covered in implementation already <ul> <li><em><span class="error">&#91;Tanya&#93;</span></em>: the actions should be available only to requestor. Interpreter should see it as a read-only - just to be notified that the call is being transcribed.</li> </ul> </li> </ul> </description>
