<comment id="126129" author="557058:bf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" created="Thu, 26 Jun 2025 08:08:06 -0500"><p><a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Ad005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" class="user-hover" rel="557058:d005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" data-account-id="557058:d005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" accountid="557058:d005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" rel="noreferrer">Tetiana Tymonina</a> should crowd interpreters see transcriptions read-only icon in their caller? Asking because showing it for them also means supporting S2S scenario (S2S interpreter is always crowd).</p></comment>
