<comment id="126488" author="557058:bf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" created="Wed, 2 Jul 2025 04:59:14 -0500"><p><a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Ad005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" class="user-hover" rel="557058:d005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" data-account-id="557058:d005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" accountid="557058:d005829d-f994-4adf-ac20-54fa72b78108" rel="noreferrer">Tetiana Tymonina</a> no they will be transcribed, and actually the only thing, which is missed for S2S is transcriptions icon in the caller header on interpreter side.</p></comment>
